2b:["$","p","3",{"children":["$","span",null,{"style":{"color":"rgb(0, 0, 0)","fontSize":"20px"},"children":"India is facing another fuel price shock as petrol and diesel prices increased by 90 paise on Tuesday, just days after a massive ₹3 per litre hike. In Delhi, petrol prices have now reached ₹98.64 per litre. With global crude oil prices crossing $111 per barrel, the continuous rise has triggered strong public concern over inflation and higher daily expenses."}]}]
